{:id :EACL-FORMAL-002
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :property
 :seed-or-trace "eacl.bench.pagination-test/recursive-traversal-prefix-benchmark"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions ["current worktree at discovery"]
 :affected-backends [:datomic]
 :root-cause
 "The v3 Datomic client unconditionally returns nil from continuation-context, so neither recursive continuations, completed recursive pages, nor acyclic frontier heads are retained. Every cursor page deterministically replays its prefix; sufficiently deep valid walks can exceed traversal limits."
 :fix
 "Datomic clients now own a bounded private continuation store. Opaque states are accepted only with an identical per-client capability and a key committing to source, adapter, identity, schema, operation, query, dependency scope, and authenticated proof. Missing state still replays the exact selected snapshot."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.datomic.lookup-cache-test/recursive-cursors-resume-private-continuations-within-client-test"
  "eacl.datomic.lookup-cache-test/recursive-cursors-replay-across-independent-client-proofs-test"
  "eacl.bench.pagination-test/recursive-traversal-prefix-benchmark"
  "eacl.bench.pagination-test/recursive-page-size-work-benchmark"]}
